{
 "about": "Hand-worked cases for docs/vin-contract.md and docs/state-contract.md §4.0. `args` are the call's arguments without D; D (datasets[data], 'T1:bad' = T1 with both tables replaced by non-arrays) goes where the contract puts it: match(dec, D), carMakes(D), carModels(D, make), carYears(D, make, model), carLookup(D, make, model, year). A case with `fixture` takes tests/fixtures/vin/vpic/<fixture>.json as its one argument.",
 "datasets": {
  "T1": {
   "CAR_DATA": [
    "Acme|Roadster:30*,Sedan:40,Volt:35e",
    "Ford|F-150 Lightning:20e,F150:21",
    "Honda|Accord:38,Civic:42",
    "Mercedes-Benz|C-Class:30*"
   ],
   "CAR_YEARS": [
    "Acme|Classic:20@2001-2003,Sedan:40@2024-2026 33@2020-2023 30@2018,Volt:35e@2025-2026",
    "Ford|F-150 Lightning:20e@2022-2025,F150:21@2024-2026 19@2018-2020",
    "Honda|Accord:38@2023-2026 33@2018-2022 24@2003",
    "Mercedes-Benz|C-Class:30*@2020-2026"
   ]
  },
  "T2": {
   "CAR_DATA": [
    "Zed|Bad:x,Good:25d",
    "Zed|Bad:31",
    5,
    "NoBar",
    "|Empty:20",
    "Zed|:20,Dup:30,Dup:40"
   ],
   "CAR_YEARS": [
    "Zed|Car:0@2020 25@2021-2020 30@20 31@2019 x 28*@2015-2017  27d@2014,Car:22@2010",
    "Tie|T:20@2019-2020 25@2018-2020",
    "Odd|O:20@2010 30@2015",
    "Mercedes Benz|C:10@2020",
    null,
    "Zed|NoColon"
   ]
  },
  "T3": {
   "CAR_DATA": [
    "Mercedes-Benz|C-Class:30*"
   ],
   "CAR_YEARS": [
    "Mercedes Benz|C:10@2020"
   ]
  }
 },
 "datasets_about": {
  "T1": "T1: Acme has Roadster and Volt in CAR_DATA, Classic only in CAR_YEARS, Sedan in both (with a 2019 gap). Honda Civic is only in CAR_DATA. Ford has F150 and F-150 Lightning, whose keys are f150 and f150lightning. Made up.",
  "T2": "T2: malformed runs and rows. 'Mercedes Benz' (a space) sorts before 'Mercedes-Benz' (0x20 < 0x2D) when both tables are merged with T1 by patch.",
  "T3": "T3: two spellings of one make key."
 },
